{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_9a76a549662b2421f785e6ccdb42c4f38db9fe766c43ed4b58f73a2b59a93389"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In local mode the guest shell runs over serial: the kernel boots with console=ttyS0 and nehemiahd pumps the Firecracker child's stdin/stdout as the terminal, working identically for cold-boot and snapshot-restored VMs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ae6737a936e8bc68260bf5dd36c5888da7c61e3071fb7c20dbde768e804bcf57"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The local daemon exposes a REST API on port 8080 (machine create/list/get/delete, branch, and a /tty WebSocket with binary frames) plus an open /healthz endpoint."}],"claim_ids":["clm_9a76a549662b2421f785e6ccdb42c4f38db9fe766c43ed4b58f73a2b59a93389","clm_ae6737a936e8bc68260bf5dd36c5888da7c61e3071fb7c20dbde768e804bcf57"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","id":"pg_49bc2e95db7d51fca09a872b75292692","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/boringcomputers-nehemiah-docs-architecture-md-fea6f0a52991-872b75292692.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_bd14f38d5319510aaa5289cafd1e81ba"],"title":"boringcomputers/nehemiah/docs/architecture.md @ fea6f0a52991","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2e3794f01aab746fc7dda899a695426344f9c6c9a78fbc6579a0ba48eafd8831"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Managed machines move through persisted lifecycle states (requested, placing, starting, running, stopping, stopped, failed, lost); terminal records never regress, and a machine declared lost is never presented as recovered."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f730ad3510737a84b75bedd0560736e078d47424bb18529a606e56cb6c785f7c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The scheduler filters hosts by region, architecture, size, template availability, health, and hard quotas, reserving capacity in one PostgreSQL transaction and preferring hosts with the requested template cached."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2e3794f01aab746fc7dda899a695426344f9c6c9a78fbc6579a0ba48eafd8831","clm_f730ad3510737a84b75bedd0560736e078d47424bb18529a606e56cb6c785f7c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","id":"pg_4fcb33c902b351a0b0088ccbd34b5161","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/boringcomputers-nehemiah-docs-nehemiah-architecture-md-fea6f0a52991-8ccbd34b5161.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6e8b487ed9c85c17a5aa3ee67e177818"],"title":"boringcomputers/nehemiah/docs/nehemiah/architecture.md @ fea6f0a52991","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2e3794f01aab746fc7dda899a695426344f9c6c9a78fbc6579a0ba48eafd8831","clm_36e37e49562b2b017ce12be1619d556474c724bd230b1c52a17f99bd2a1ada70","clm_616922b72dacd88ed2014b9ecf1c50ce4239a640098c3e2837e8098b0eb00d73","clm_6b0e262d57faa44b56d27264b0a2bbe7ef8c715c3f5fcd150ed319347f33d110","clm_7170227d3bda5cb1fdc4dc7708451a7879aa84ad27d64922ec960c1d430e7bfa","clm_7c6e2a602675cae366b0be89cf922f8135be106869c65a19921311896fa5adf1","clm_8ce63f73fc921269d564c3fb8a18964c6ca7e74625abbc3e7eb1671dd9146aaa","clm_9a76a549662b2421f785e6ccdb42c4f38db9fe766c43ed4b58f73a2b59a93389","clm_ae6737a936e8bc68260bf5dd36c5888da7c61e3071fb7c20dbde768e804bcf57","clm_d3919cbdc044126fbc9daea90f000aa2f1855cd501eefc732da80825d116b3a4","clm_f730ad3510737a84b75bedd0560736e078d47424bb18529a606e56cb6c785f7c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"boringcomputers/nehemiah is mentioned in this evidence."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2e3794f01aab746fc7dda899a695426344f9c6c9a78fbc6579a0ba48eafd8831","clm_36e37e49562b2b017ce12be1619d556474c724bd230b1c52a17f99bd2a1ada70","clm_616922b72dacd88ed2014b9ecf1c50ce4239a640098c3e2837e8098b0eb00d73","clm_6b0e262d57faa44b56d27264b0a2bbe7ef8c715c3f5fcd150ed319347f33d110","clm_7170227d3bda5cb1fdc4dc7708451a7879aa84ad27d64922ec960c1d430e7bfa","clm_7c6e2a602675cae366b0be89cf922f8135be106869c65a19921311896fa5adf1","clm_8ce63f73fc921269d564c3fb8a18964c6ca7e74625abbc3e7eb1671dd9146aaa","clm_9a76a549662b2421f785e6ccdb42c4f38db9fe766c43ed4b58f73a2b59a93389","clm_ae6737a936e8bc68260bf5dd36c5888da7c61e3071fb7c20dbde768e804bcf57","clm_d3919cbdc044126fbc9daea90f000aa2f1855cd501eefc732da80825d116b3a4","clm_f730ad3510737a84b75bedd0560736e078d47424bb18529a606e56cb6c785f7c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","id":"pg_5026085c462f5a9a835d55aae9eb4184","maturity":"draft","page_type":"entity","path":"pages/entities/boringcomputers-nehemiah-55aae9eb4184.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":[],"title":"boringcomputers/nehemiah","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_616922b72dacd88ed2014b9ecf1c50ce4239a640098c3e2837e8098b0eb00d73"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors use npm workspaces commands (npm run dev/build/check/lint) and are pointed to CONTRIBUTING.md; a route-inventory test fails if the exported OpenAPI contract drifts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b0e262d57faa44b56d27264b0a2bbe7ef8c715c3f5fcd150ed319347f33d110"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Managed OCI image import/pull is not implemented: requests receive a typed 501 not_supported response, and the field is documented only as a deprecated reserved field."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8ce63f73fc921269d564c3fb8a18964c6ca7e74625abbc3e7eb1671dd9146aaa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Managed host-local LLM agents are not implemented; agent-capability session issuance fails with typed not_supported, and users are directed to run agents inside the guest via exec/TTY/file primitives."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d3919cbdc044126fbc9daea90f000aa2f1855cd501eefc732da80825d116b3a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"File access uses capability-scoped session tokens sent only as bearer headers; query tokens, cookies, and redirects are forbidden, uploads are capped at 16 MiB, and sessions can be revoked with a typed DELETE endpoint."}],"claim_ids":["clm_616922b72dacd88ed2014b9ecf1c50ce4239a640098c3e2837e8098b0eb00d73","clm_6b0e262d57faa44b56d27264b0a2bbe7ef8c715c3f5fcd150ed319347f33d110","clm_8ce63f73fc921269d564c3fb8a18964c6ca7e74625abbc3e7eb1671dd9146aaa","clm_d3919cbdc044126fbc9daea90f000aa2f1855cd501eefc732da80825d116b3a4"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","id":"pg_653b9df7764a5bddbb5fc7f87ce65032","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/boringcomputers-nehemiah-docs-nehemiah-api-contract-md-fea6f0a52991-c7f87ce65032.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_3f90deb4003b5c8e84e129b05844b381"],"title":"boringcomputers/nehemiah/docs/nehemiah/api-contract.md @ fea6f0a52991","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_36e37e49562b2b017ce12be1619d556474c724bd230b1c52a17f99bd2a1ada70"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each machine is a hardware-virtualized Firecracker microVM with its own kernel, jailed and resource-capped, restored from a memory snapshot in milliseconds, with guests network-isolated behind an egress firewall."},{"claim_ids":["clm_616922b72dacd88ed2014b9ecf1c50ce4239a640098c3e2837e8098b0eb00d73"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors use npm workspaces commands (npm run dev/build/check/lint) and are pointed to CONTRIBUTING.md; a route-inventory test fails if the exported OpenAPI contract drifts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7170227d3bda5cb1fdc4dc7708451a7879aa84ad27d64922ec960c1d430e7bfa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An MCP server package (nehemiah-mcp) lets clients like Claude Desktop and Cursor spin up and drive Nehemiah computers as a tool, configured via npx with a NEHEMIAH_URL env var."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7c6e2a602675cae366b0be89cf922f8135be106869c65a19921311896fa5adf1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repo is a Turborepo/npm-workspaces monorepo: apps/web (SvelteKit site), nehemiahd (Go host daemon), packages/sdk (Effect-native TypeScript client), packages/mcp, and infra/latitude provisioning."}],"claim_ids":["clm_36e37e49562b2b017ce12be1619d556474c724bd230b1c52a17f99bd2a1ada70","clm_616922b72dacd88ed2014b9ecf1c50ce4239a640098c3e2837e8098b0eb00d73","clm_7170227d3bda5cb1fdc4dc7708451a7879aa84ad27d64922ec960c1d430e7bfa","clm_7c6e2a602675cae366b0be89cf922f8135be106869c65a19921311896fa5adf1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca","id":"pg_85b9751b17865fd0aa468a9825812a31","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/boringcomputers-nehemiah-readme-md-fea6f0a52991-8a9825812a31.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_98ba94c2a3d259a7b62a3161e96047a2"],"title":"boringcomputers/nehemiah/README.md @ fea6f0a52991","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:33Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac83769c39cc487f925292aee1794aca"}
